<title>JAPAN: Japan, EU, US welcome recent forex moves - Sakakibara.</title>
<headline>Japan, EU, US welcome recent forex moves - Sakakibara.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eisuke Sakakibara, director-general of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Finance Bureau, said on Thursday that Japan, the U.S. and EU nations welcome recent moves in the foreign exchange market as being along fundamental economic lines.</p>
<p>Speaking in a television interview, the influential official said &quot;The moves in the foreign exchange market this past year follow economic fundamentals, and the United States, the EU and Japan welcome this.&quot;</p>
<p>He added that authorities should not try to fight the market when exchange rates are mirroring economic fundamentals.</p>
</text>
